{"id": "EUVD-2026-32786", "enisaUuid": "b38a2467-f270-3467-ab0a-b77e78fed008", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: fix btrfs_ioctl_space_info() slot_count TOCTOU which can lead to info-leak\n\nbtrfs_ioctl_space_info() has a TOCTOU race between two passes over the\nblock group RAID type lists. The first pass counts entries to determine\nthe allocation size, then the second pass fills the buffer. The\ngroups_sem rwlock is released between passes, allowing concurrent block\ngroup removal to reduce the entry count.\n\nWhen the second pass fills fewer entries than the first pass counted,\ncopy_to_user() copies the full alloc_size bytes including trailing\nuninitialized kmalloc bytes to userspace.\n\nFix by copying only total_spaces entries (the actually-filled count from\nthe second pass) instead of alloc_size bytes, and switch to kzalloc so\nany future copy size mismatch cannot leak heap data.", "datePublished": "2026-05-28T09:36:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:20:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f407aad350bdea4db300c47433573b7a41630d33", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8224b1be6627c6c3b204bfb264508d27c65ac44", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d69a4a6813fdba7c4cc3695a7e843842b240790d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5ee467b56764964027c361641f64953fc0f8f9a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fdc6ee0802121d9cd96b8d085e589f51e5a4ec3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d12e0ab009ade48c1bff9324fd9bea2c773d088", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d09d67d5de577cedae3de9497dff217e0ac8b641", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/973e57c726c1f8e77259d1c8e519519f1e9aea77"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8m37-fqxx-cfwj", "CVE-2026-46159"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c6ede17-bcc6-3047-805d-c48f80de5e73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fde62bffb576d384ea49a3aed3403d5609ee5bc <d69a4a6813fdba7c4cc3695a7e843842b240790d"}, {"id": "164f0953-9219-32f7-9967-e0579458629a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fde62bffb576d384ea49a3aed3403d5609ee5bc <f5ee467b56764964027c361641f64953fc0f8f9a"}, {"id": "17bc0221-8e0f-3b8d-9e13-ea8bcb0a7735", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "1d76d883-69c6-3e8a-9c23-e8b3419f90c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.176"}, {"id": "3859b995-1849-38a4-977e-6adf477b3f92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.7"}, {"id": "4eb15967-d595-3c53-b569-d1e96cd6ee0a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.259"}, {"id": "53e60861-21bd-382a-9fdd-b893f2fc3fbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fde62bffb576d384ea49a3aed3403d5609ee5bc <d09d67d5de577cedae3de9497dff217e0ac8b641"}, {"id": "54e62559-e2b2-34af-b05c-6eb542da87f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.90"}, {"id": "5a945e2f-f6fb-30e2-b92b-cddc9ecdb120", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fde62bffb576d384ea49a3aed3403d5609ee5bc <973e57c726c1f8e77259d1c8e519519f1e9aea77"}, {"id": "a5373558-71a8-3e30-8496-6ddc6dfccab9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fde62bffb576d384ea49a3aed3403d5609ee5bc <5d12e0ab009ade48c1bff9324fd9bea2c773d088"}, {"id": "b08b9ae9-add2-303e-81a3-9f0d12a05ee6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.140"}, {"id": "c0d85d9e-1d12-301e-8c8d-ae6aee06149e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.32"}, {"id": "cf9b6fb1-decf-38ae-bbc7-f681e9ba0b7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fde62bffb576d384ea49